WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.450
- I wrote an open letter
in Pollstar this year,

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.350
which is like the touring magazine,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.260
and I had just had this situation

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.470
where for the first time,

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.460
I've got my wife who's pregnant

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.460
with another little girl

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.293
and I'm like thinking,

00:00:11.293 --> 00:00:13.370
I seeing how different
my wife's experience

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.230
is to mine.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.524
Just like, very, very,
drastically different

00:00:16.524 --> 00:00:17.920
- First of all, thank
you for paying attention.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.210
- Completely different.
- Yeah.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.780
- So then I'm thinking about that on tour

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.610
and I'm like, man, I've never just asked

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:24.827
the women on my tour,

00:00:24.827 --> 00:00:27.120
"What can I do differently
for you on this tour?"

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.380
So I got 'em all together in a room,

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.577
and I was just like,
"Hey, is there anything

00:00:29.577 --> 00:00:30.717
"different I can do?

00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:32.357
"Is there anything different for women

00:00:32.357 --> 00:00:33.647
"that I can do to make this better?"

00:00:33.647 --> 00:00:34.480
- That I'm not thinking of.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.850
- That I'm not think of.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.540
And they gave me a couple things

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:38.373
that could be done better.

00:00:38.373 --> 00:00:41.120
One of 'em was trash cans on the tour bus

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.000
with lids.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.990
(audience laughing)
Because,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.160
I would never have thought of that.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.160
- Yeah, but just so you
know, like, you know,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.890
sometimes we have a certain time of month,

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.010
and you want a lid on the trash can.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.010
- That's what I'm saying.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.220
And I never knew it, like,

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.000
that would have never crossed my mind.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:54.833
- Well, you don't wear tampons.

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:56.182
- Exactly, I don't wear tampons.

00:00:56.182 --> 00:00:57.015
(audience laughing)

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:58.910
- Unless you do, I don't know!

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.570
- So they go around and
they each share something

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.830
that could be helpful

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.840
and then they each went around

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.387
and said, like, "No one's
asked me this before."

00:01:07.387 --> 00:01:08.510
- Yeah.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:10.197
- And I'm just like, "What?

00:01:10.197 --> 00:01:11.447
"No one's ever asked you this before.

00:01:11.447 --> 00:01:12.280
"That's insane.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.227
"You guys have all been touring forever.

00:01:13.227 --> 00:01:14.880
"How has this not happened?"

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.280
And then I'm looking back at myself.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.460
I've been touring for eight years.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.570
I've never asked you this before.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:21.020
What the hell is going on?

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.900
Why, what's the disconnect?

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.010
Like, I think I'm a good guy

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.900
and I've never asked you this before.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.269
So then I'm like, man, I gotta share this

00:01:28.269 --> 00:01:30.790
and I wrote this open letter

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.660
and tried to share it in
the touring community.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.700
You know my mom was an amazing woman

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.020
who helped to, tried to empower

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.280
as many women as possible.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.030
And she would always read this quote to me

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.706
about that the world of humanity is like,

00:01:40.706 --> 00:01:43.750
has two wings, male and female,

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:44.910
and unless they're both strong

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.410
the bird can't fly.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.243
So--

00:01:47.243 --> 00:01:48.076
- You're mom is great!

00:01:48.076 --> 00:01:49.255
She's dope, she's really dope.

00:01:49.255 --> 00:01:50.088
- Wow!

00:01:50.088 --> 00:01:50.921
- And

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.070
it's like not revolutionary

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.780
but when men stick up for women

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.140
with a pure intent it
just makes me emotional.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.420
But, it's really important

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.310
and there's not enough of it.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:02.260
- And why you're getting emotional

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.630
is 'cause you now have,

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.160
you have a baby girl.
- I've got two girls.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.320
- Yeah, a baby girl.
- Yeah, I have two girls.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.887
Yeah, it's important.

